  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.20: PDF Unicode fallback chain. #75: the single DejaVu Sans fallback is now an ordered chain (primary embedded -> DejaVu Sans -> Symbola), bundling Symbola (public domain) as a secondary symbol font. Symbols outside DejaVu's coverage (e.g. SMP blocks like U+1F6C7) now render in the PDF instead of '?', matching the Avalonia preview. DejaVu remains the general/text fallback; Symbola is consulted only for glyphs DejaVu lacks and is subset + embedded only when actually used. See CHANGELOG.md.",
